    "solution": "\\(\\cos B=\\tfrac{c^2+a^2-b^2}{2ac}=\\tfrac{ac}{2ac}=\\tfrac12\\Rightarrow B=\\tfrac{\\pi}{3}\\)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c183c893-0a67-4083-a518-e2ec174c4835",
    "ref": "Misc I Q.9",
    "derived_answer": "A",
    "solution": "\\(a\\cos B=\\tfrac{a^2+c^2-b^2}{2c}\\), \\(b\\cos A=\\tfrac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2c}\\); so \\(ac\\cos B-bc\\cos A=c(a\\cos B-b\\cos A)=c\\cdot\\tfrac{a^2-b^2}{c}=a^2-b^2\\)."
  },
