    "solution": "\\(\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac13+\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac12=\\tan^{-1}\\tfrac{1/3+1/2}{1-1/6}=\\tan^{-1}1=\\tfrac{\\pi}{4}\\); \\(\\cos\\tfrac{\\pi}{4}=\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\)."
  },
  {
    "id": "0dd998ff-51e1-4dd8-a1fa-7481002a34e8",
    "ref": "Misc I Q.19",
    "derived_answer": "A",
    "solution": "The equation reduces to \\(\\tan\\theta+\\tan2\\theta=0\\Rightarrow\\tan\\theta(3-\\tan^2\\theta)=0\\), giving \\(\\tan\\theta=0\\) or \\(\\tan\\theta=\\pm\\sqrt3\\), i.e. the full set \\(\\theta=\\tfrac{n\\pi}{3}\\). NONE of the options equals \\(\\tfrac{n\\pi}{3}\\); best pick is A \\((n\\pi)\\), which is the valid \\(\\tan\\theta=0\\) sub-branch (all such \\(\\theta\\) are genuine solutions), whereas B \\(\\tfrac{n\\pi}{6}\\) includes points where \\(\\tan3\\theta\\) is undefined."
  },
  {
